{# Public safety notice band for the Today board.

   Renders nothing at all when no notice is live, so it is safe to leave
   in place permanently — the whole block disappears from the HTML rather
   than collapsing to an empty box.

   Deliberately NOT styled as an alarm. This is a town noticeboard, not an
   emergency broadcast: a calm band that says what to look for and what to
   do. Red banners and warning triangles train people to ignore them, and
   the audience here skews older and is easily alarmed by the visual
   language of emergency.

   The link goes to the item in the register, so the notice is always
   traceable to the meeting where it was raised. #}

{% set live = notice.notices | currentNotices %}
{% if live | length %}
{% for n in live %}
<section class="wrap notice-band" aria-labelledby="notice-h">
  <div class="notice-inner">
    <p class="notice-kicker">Public safety notice</p>
    <h2 class="notice-title" id="notice-h">{{ n.title }}</h2>
    <p class="notice-body">{{ n.body }}</p>
    {% if n.sourceUrl %}
    <p class="notice-source"><a href="{{ n.sourceUrl }}">Where this came from →</a></p>
    {% endif %}
  </div>
</section>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
